  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling up the KOCP community-based Elephant Conservation Unit to better understand elephant ecology in man-made landscapes and mitigate raising conflicts with people.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to expand the range of an existing community-based Elephant Conservation Unit (ECU) to reach communities recently experiencing human-elephant conflict (HEC) as well as collect Asian elephant behavioral and socioecological data in agricultural landscapes in Sabah, Malaysia. Four additional members will be added to the ECU and their range will be increased to cover additional districts. Project activities include: 1) direct observations of Asian elephant herds within agricultural landscapes (especially oil palm), habitat assessments, and assessments of elephant-related damages; 2) identification and training of community members in HEC-affected villages; 3) surveys of local communities, and education and awareness events; 4) law enforcement patrols via an Honorary Wildlife Warden Program; and 5) contributing to the development of policy documents and strategies to manage Asian elephants and their ranges in Sabah. This project will contribute to the conservation of wild Asian elephant populations in Sabah by increasing knowledge of elephant ecology outside of protected areas, reducing HEC levels in areas with relatively new HEC activity, and contributing to efforts to better manage Sabahs wild elephants by informing policy and land-use decision-making by policymakers.</narrative>
  </description>
